# MFP1-2992: supply-chain cooldown. Refuse dependency versions published less
# than two days ago, so a malicious release has time to be detected and yanked
# before it can reach a build.
#
# The unit here is DAYS, unlike pnpm and Yarn, which take minutes.
#
# Requires npm >= 11.10.0. Older npm silently ignores this key rather than
# failing, so the setting is not self-enforcing -- see the ADR in
# development-adrs for the minimum package manager versions.
#
# Note that `npm ci` installs exactly what the lockfile pins and ignores this
# key entirely. The Dependabot `cooldown` is what governs lockfile updates.
#
# Do not pass `--before` on the same npm invocation; the two options conflict.
min-release-age=2
